// @name         Metadata Scrubber — Strip EXIF/XMP/GPS/PDF/ZIP/HTML/TXT info before upload (Firefox)
// @namespace    cleanroom.privacy
// @version      2.8.1
// @description  Intercepts file uploads (file inputs incl. detached/shadow-DOM ones, drag&drop, clipboard paste, native form submits, FormData, fetch, XHR, sendBeacon, WebSocket/RTCDataChannel, WebTransport (best-effort), raw ArrayBuffer/Request bodies) and strips identifying metadata from JPEG/PNG/WebP/GIF/JP2/PDF, plain ZIP archives (recursively), HTML and TXT files before any byte leaves the machine. Optional per-site "auto convert" switch (in the Tampermonkey menu) re-encodes WebP uploads as JPG or PNG when that is smaller. 100% client-side, zero network calls.
